{:schema_version 1
 :changes
 [{:id "workers-ai-usage-captions"
   :date "2026-11-01"
   :component "app"
   :title "Workers AI captions show priced usage"
   :summary "Gemma token usage is estimated at Cloudflare's published model rates. Unknown Workers AI prices show reported neurons or input/output tokens instead of an invented cost. Zen free-usage rejections identify the upstream limit and numeric retry delay; denied access does not trigger paid fallback or client impersonation."
   :commands ["ai --provider cloudflare --model @cf/google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it Hello"
              "zen Hello"]
   :requires ["Configured provider credentials and upstream model access"]
   :links []}
  {:id "runtime-ai-defaults"
   :date "2026-11-01"
   :component "app"
   :title "Admins can change global AI defaults at runtime"
   :summary "Inspect, set or reset the global AI provider/model without editing configuration or restarting. Changes require a trusted admin and retain normal tool policy; explicit request flags win. Runtime choices reset on restart. Zen defaults remain freshly verified-free, while an explicit admin choice may select a paid model on another configured provider."
   :commands ["ai default" "ai default <provider> <model>" "ai default reset"]
   :requires ["Existing configured AI provider" "Admin authorization for changes"]
   :links []}
  {:id "free-zen-defaults"
   :date "2026-11-01"
   :component "app"
   :title "Zen defaults follow currently free offerings"
   :summary "Zen defaults verify current zero input, output and advertised cache pricing before selection. Expired offers are not retained; unknown or paid pricing fails closed. Trusted admins can set a free Zen preference through the global runtime AI default controls. Explicit --model remains an intentional choice, including paid models. Catalog eligibility does not prove access: rate or quota limits can still reject inference."
   :commands ["zen Say hello" "ai --provider zen Say hello"]
   :requires ["Configured Zen credentials and upstream model access"]
   :links []}
  {:id "tiny-discord-ai-captions"
   :date "2026-11-01"
   :component "app"
   :title "Small Discord AI captions"
   :summary "Discord AI and Zen answers use muted subtext for the model, measured execution time and known host-tool count. Cost labels distinguish provider-reported API totals, usage-based token estimates, fresh-free Zen estimates and stable live Grok visible-text estimates. Missing or incomplete cost is marked unavailable, never invented zero; Slack formatting is unchanged."
   :commands ["ai Hello" "grok Hello"]
   :requires ["Discord"]
   :links []}
  {:id "release-discovery"
   :date "2026-10-31"
   :component "app"
   :title "Ask Yetibot what's new"
   :summary "Read the running app and core versions, browse bundled feature notes, or ask AI to explain them using a read-only release_info tool. Published JSON mirrors the same release data; a latest lookup is separate from what's installed."
   :commands ["version" "changelog" "ai show me the new yetibot features"]
   :requires []
   :links []}
  {:id "native-discord-reactions"
   :date "2026-10-31"
   :component "app"
   :title "AI can react to Discord messages"
   :summary "The native react tool adds a Unicode or custom-emoji reaction in the original channel or thread. By default it targets the human message that requested the response. It cannot change channels or remove reactions."
   :commands ["ai react to this message with a thumbs up"]
   :requires ["Discord and an authorized native AI toolset"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/yetibot/pull/1292"]}
  {:id "opencode-zen"
   :date "2026-10-31"
   :component "app"
   :title "Discover and use OpenCode Zen models"
   :summary "zen models lists advertised model IDs. zen sends a bounded text-only request; ai --provider zen retains the normal AI context and tools. Bare zen now shows usage, not GitHub wisdom. Default selection now follows currently verified-free offerings without a paid fallback."
   :commands ["zen" "zen models" "zen --model MODEL PROMPT"
              "ai --provider zen --model MODEL PROMPT"]
   :requires ["OpenCode credentials and inference entitlement"
              "An explicit or configured model; advertised pricing does not prove access"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/yetibot/pull/1289"
           "https://github.com/yetibot/yetibot/pull/1292"]}
  {:id "unicode-and-custom-reactions"
   :date "2026-10-31"
   :component "core"
   :title "React with Unicode and custom Discord emoji"
   :summary "Reaction parsing supports static and animated custom emoji, Unicode symbols, subdivision flags and newer emoji. Bot-added reactions are ignored by reaction observers to avoid feedback and accidental self-deletion."
   :commands ["react 👍"]
   :requires ["Discord for custom emoji"]
   :links ["https://github.com/yetibot/core/pull/328"
           "https://github.com/yetibot/core/pull/329"]}
  {:id "readable-tables-and-long-answers"
   :date "2026-10-31"
   :component "core"
   :title "Readable tables and longer Discord answers"
   :summary "Components V2 replies fit up to 4,000 rendered characters. Markdown tables become aligned code blocks. Longer answers and unsafe or oversized tables include a readable excerpt and an exact answer.md download. Image captions use the same formatter."
